# DAO & Home Patterns — Lutece 8

## DAO Class

- `@ApplicationScoped public class EntityDAO implements IEntityDAO` — resolved through its interface. `final` is allowed (core and forms DAOs are `final`) as long as nothing resolves the concrete class (`@Inject EntityDAO`, `select( EntityDAO.class )`).
- `@Named( "plugin.entityDAO" )` only when a producer or a `NamedLiteral` lookup resolves the bean by name (workflow `ITaskConfigDAO` producers). Default: no `@Named`.
- SQL constants: `SQL_QUERY_SELECT`, `SQL_QUERY_INSERT`, `SQL_QUERY_UPDATE`, `SQL_QUERY_DELETE`, `SQL_QUERY_SELECTALL`. No `SQL_QUERY_NEWPK` / `SELECT max( id )`.
- Primary key: `AUTO_INCREMENT` column + `new DAOUtil( SQL_QUERY_INSERT, Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS, plugin )`, then `if ( daoUtil.nextGeneratedKey( ) ) entity.setId( daoUtil.getGeneratedKeyInt( 1 ) );`
- DAOUtil ALWAYS with try-with-resources: `try ( DAOUtil daoUtil = new DAOUtil( SQL_QUERY, plugin ) )`
- Parameters are **1-indexed**, use `nIndex++` for sequential access
- The getter and setter match the column type of the create script: `getInt`/`setInt` on a `varchar` column throws `cannot be decoded as Integer` on a non-numeric value (MariaDB driver) and casts every row on a bound number (no index). A v7 id column declared as text is changed with an upgrade script, never in the create script alone (DA03).
- `executeUpdate()` for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE, `executeQuery()` for SELECT
- `daoUtil.next()` with `if` for single row, `while` for collections

## Home — Static Facade

- `private static IEntityDAO _dao = CDI.current().select( IEntityDAO.class ).get();` — the static field initializer is the idiom (core `RoleHome`, forms `FormHome`)
- `private static Plugin _plugin = PluginService.getPlugin( "pluginname" );`
- Private constructor, all methods static
- Methods: `create`, `update`, `remove`, `findByPrimaryKey`, `findAll`, plus finders per need (`findReferenceList` only when a `<select>` needs it)
- NEVER declare a `BEAN_xxx_DAO` / `DAO_BEAN_NAME` string constant — the typesafe `CDI.current().select( IEntityDAO.class )` lookup makes it dead code
- NEVER a `getInstance( )`: a Home has no instance (HM01)

## Portlet Home — CDI bean

A class extending `PortletHome` is an object (the core calls `getDAO( )`, `getPortletTypeId( )` on it), in the CDI form
(HM02):

- `@ApplicationScoped`, not `final`, no static instance of itself
- `public static PortletHome getInstance( ) { return CDI.current( ).select( XPortletHome.class ).get( ); }`

The core also creates it by reflection (`Class.forName( ).getDeclaredConstructor( ).newInstance( )`), so whatever its
form (HM01, these break):

- a public no-arg constructor
- its DAO in a static field from `CDI.current( ).select( IXPortletDAO.class ).get( )`, never an `@Inject` field (the
  instance the core creates is never injected)

A hand-made singleton still works: HM02 asks for the CDI form.

## Interface

Every DAO has an `IEntityDAO` interface with `insert`, `load`, `store`, `delete`, `selectAll` and its custom finders. All methods take `Plugin plugin` as last parameter. A `ReferenceList selectXxxReferenceList` exists only when a dropdown needs it.

## Return Types

- `List<Entity>` for standard lists
- `ReferenceList` for dropdowns (`<select>`)
- `Optional<Entity>` for optional single results

## One-shot action: the guard is in the WHERE

An action that must run once (validate, pay, send) is claimed by the `UPDATE` itself, never by a `SELECT` then an
`UPDATE`: two concurrent requests both read "not done" and both proceed. The DAO returns whether this call won:

```java
private static final String SQL_QUERY_MARK_AS_COMPLETE = "UPDATE x_response SET is_complete = 1 WHERE id_response = ? AND is_complete = 0";

public boolean markAsComplete( int nIdResponse, Plugin plugin )
{
    try ( DAOUtil daoUtil = new DAOUtil( SQL_QUERY_MARK_AS_COMPLETE, plugin ) )
    {
        daoUtil.setInt( 1, nIdResponse );
        daoUtil.executeUpdate( );
        return daoUtil.getReturnedRowCount( ) > 0;
    }
}
```

The service side (claim first, compensate on failure) is in `service-layer.md`.

## Transactions: the caller's transaction wins

- Inside a `@Transactional` method (JTA, pool `Managed`), `DAOUtil` joins the container's transaction by itself
  (`ITransactionSynchronizationManager.isSynchronizationActive( )`). A Home that also opens
  `TransactionManager.beginTransaction` there commits, rolls back and changes auto-commit on a connection enlisted in the
  global transaction: `DSRA9250E ... not allowed during a global transaction`, logged on every call.
- A Home called both from a `@Transactional` service and on its own detects the caller's transaction and then neither
  commits nor rolls back, as core `FileHome.isJoiningExistingTransaction( )` does.

## Row created on first use by concurrent requests

Never insert, then catch the duplicate key: `DAOUtil` turns every `SQLException` into an `AppException`, which logs a
`Critical AppException` even when the caller recovers. Create the row with its parent (when the entity is created), or
create it in the transaction that uses it, after locking the parent row (genericattributes `EntryNumberingDAO`:
`SELECT id_entry FROM genatt_entry WHERE id_entry = ? FOR UPDATE`, then read again, then insert).

A list of rows loaded by id from a type the site may not have (portlets of an uninstalled plugin) skips the ids the
Home cannot load: `PortletHome.findByPrimaryKey( )` returns `null` when the class of the portlet type cannot be loaded.

## Existing JPA Model

Kept on the `jakarta.persistence` API, provider EclipseLink of the container (`persistence-3.1`, `persistence.xml` in JTA on `jdbc/portal`, `shared-cache-mode NONE`), no `org.hibernate` import, `DAOUtil` and `EntityManager` mixed only under `@Transactional` with `ManagedConnectionService`. Rules: `skills/lutece-update-plugin/patterns/persistence-patterns.md`.

